lesson: 154
title: The calendar: days from one month into the next
level: primary-3
stars: 1
explain: April, June, September and November have 30 days; the other months have 31, except February.
explain: To count the days from a date in one month to a date in the next, count the days left to the end of the first month, then add the date in the second month.
explain: From the 25th of April to the 6th of May: 30 - 25 = 5 days to the end of April, then 6 more days, 5 + 6 = 11 days.
vars: a=name d=2..29 e=1..28
need: 30 - d + e >= 3
answer: 30 - d + e
exercise: {a} leaves for camp on the {d.ord} of June and comes back on the {e.ord} of July. How many days after leaving does {a.he} come back?
exercise: Today is the {d.ord} of April. {a}'s birthday is on the {e.ord} of May. In how many days is the birthday?
exercise: A seed was planted on the {d.ord} of September, and the plant had its first flower on the {e.ord} of October. How many days did that take?
exercise: The school holidays begin on the {d.ord} of November, and the trip is on the {e.ord} of December. How many days after the start of the holidays is the trip?
exercise: How many days are there from the {d.ord} of June to the {e.ord} of July?
test: How many days after April {d} is May {e}?
test: A letter sent on the {d.ord} of June arrived on the {e.ord} of July. How many days was it on the way?
test: {a} borrowed a book on November {d} and gave it back on December {e}. For how many days did {a.he} keep it?
test: It is the {d.ord} of September. A concert will be held on the {e.ord} of October. How many days are left until the concert?
exercise: How many days are there from April {d} to May {e}?
exercise: {a} flew to Canada on the {d.ord} of June and flew home on the {e.ord} of July. How many days after flying out did {a.he} fly home?
exercise: A library book in Boston was taken out on September {d} and returned on October {e}. How many days was it out?
exercise: The {d.ord} of November is today, and a school fair in Dublin is on the {e.ord} of December. How many days from today is the fair?
exercise: Count the days from the {d.ord} of September to the {e.ord} of October.
exercise: {a} started a jigsaw puzzle on the {d.ord} of April and finished it on the {e.ord} of May. How many days later did {a.he} finish?
exercise: A sailing boat left Sydney on June {d} and reached Fiji on July {e}. How many days did the voyage take?
exercise: Eggs were put under a hen on the {d.ord} of April, and the chicks hatched on the {e.ord} of May. How many days did that take?
test: If today is the {d.ord} of June, how many days is it until the {e.ord} of July?
test: A parcel posted in London on September {d} reached Toronto on October {e}. How many days did it travel?
test: {a} went to stay with {a.his} grandmother in Scotland on November {d} and left on December {e}. How many days after arriving did {a.he} leave?
test: The {d.ord} of April and the {e.ord} of May: how many days apart are these two dates?
test: How many days pass between September {d} and October {e}?
test: A plant in a classroom in Ohio was watered on the {d.ord} of November and then not again until the {e.ord} of December. How many days went by between the waterings?
exercise: camp: leave {d.ord} June, back {e.ord} July. how many days after leaving is that
exercise: today's {d.ord} April, bday's {e.ord} May. how many days to go
exercise: my mate says June {d} to July {e} is {e+31-d} days cos every month's 31. nah June's 30. how many days
exercise: nan's coming June {d+1}, no wait, June {d}, and goes July {e}. how many days after she comes does she go
test: April {d} to May {e}, how many days is that
test: {a}'s hols start June {d}, back at school July {e}, and it rained 4 of them days ugh. how many days from start to back
test: it's April {d-1}, no wait, it's the {d.ord}. party's May {e}. how many days to wait
exam: It is given that {a} departed for camp on the {d.ord} of June and returned on the {e.ord} of July. Determine the number of days elapsing between the departure and the return.
exam: Whereas the present date is the {d.ord} of April and the birthday of {a} falls on the {e.ord} of May, ascertain the number of days remaining until the said birthday.
exam: Ascertain the number of days from the {d.ord} of September to the {e.ord} of October of the same year.
exam: A notice issued on the {d.ord} of November states that the library shall reopen on the {e.ord} of December. State the number of days that shall elapse between the issue of the notice and the reopening.
exercise: {a}'s mum was let go on the {d.ord} of June and started a new job on the {e.ord} of July. For how many days was she between jobs?
exercise: The old cat was put to sleep on the {d.ord} of April, and the new kitten came home on the {e.ord} of May. How many days after that sad day did the kitten come?
test: {a} "misremembered" when the library book was due, the lying toad. borrowed it the {d.ord} of June, took it back the {e.ord} of July. how many days did {a.he} have it
